{"id": "6048f8dc-c851-4b14-8062-ff2fc5c348b4", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll review the auroradataapi cluster in us-east-1 for Serverless v2 capacity, storage and I/O configuration, and snapshots. The review is read-only and limited to that cluster. I'll send the results back here when it finishes.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_ZQhRRObCXv23sKphy1Yr1W", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "aurora-cost-review", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["exploring-metrics"], "prompt": "{
  "task": "Read-only RDS cost optimization review of ONE Aurora cluster, covering ONLY: (1) Serverless v2 capacity, (2) storage and I/O configuration, (3) snapshots.",
  "context": "User wants findings returned in chat. STRICT SCOPE: only cluster 'auroradataapi' ([redacted ARN]), account 012345678901_1, region us-east-1. Do NOT describe, list or scan any other cluster, instance, or region. When calling describe/list APIs, always filter by this cluster identifier (e.g. db-cluster-id filter / DBClusterIdentifier) and discard anything else. Do not make any mutating calls. Current time is 2026-11-19T11:51:09Z.",
  "resources": ["[redacted ARN]", "member DB instances of this cluster only"],
  "timeframe": "Metrics: last 14 days (2026-11-05T11:51:09Z to 2026-11-19T11:51:09Z), use daily/hourly periods as appropriate; also check last 30 days for ACU and storage trends if feasible.",
  "criteria": "1) Serverless v2 capacity: ServerlessV2ScalingConfiguration MinCapacity/MaxCapacity; ServerlessDatabaseCapacity, ACUUtilization, CPUUtilization, FreeableMemory per member instance; whether min ACU is higher than needed (always-on cost), whether max is oversized, whether auto-pause (min 0) is applicable/appropriate, instance mix (provisioned vs db.serverless writer/readers), idle or underused readers, and engine version considerations. Estimate approximate cost impact where possible. 2) Storage and I/O: storage type (Aurora Standard vs Aurora I/O-Optimized), VolumeBytesUsed, VolumeReadIOPs, VolumeWriteIOPs trend; compare I/O charges vs instance/storage cost to judge whether Standard or I/O-Optimized is cheaper (I/O-Optimized generally pays off when I/O spend exceeds ~25% of total Aurora spend); storage encryption, backtrack, Performance Insights retention, enhanced monitoring, log exports and Data API only where they affect cost. 3) Snapshots: all manual and automated cluster snapshots for this cluster only (DescribeDBClusterSnapshots with DBClusterIdentifier filter) plus backup retention period; list count, age, size, snapshot type, orphaned/old manual snapshots, snapshots from deleted clusters that reference this identifier, and any cluster snapshot copies/shares; flag retention that is longer than necessary and unused snapshots that could be deleted (recommend only, do not delete). Return a concise structured report: current configuration facts, findings with evidence (metric values), estimated savings direction (high/medium/low), and prioritized recommendations. Clearly state anything you could not check due to permissions or missing data."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Review Aurora cluster auroradataapi cost: Serverless v2, storage/I/O, snapshots"}], "created_at": null}

